{"id":259,"name":"marshtomp","speciesId":259,"dex":259,"form":"normal","generation":3,"types":["water","ground"],"stats":{"hp":70,"attack":85,"defense":70,"special-attack":60,"special-defense":70,"speed":50},"abilities":[{"name":"torrent","hidden":false},{"name":"damp","hidden":true}],"height":7,"weight":280,"baseExp":142,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/259.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/259.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/259.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/259.ogg","genus":"Mud Fish Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Peixe Lama","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"The surface of MARSHTOMP’s body is enveloped by a thin, sticky film that enables it to live on land. This POKéMON plays in mud on beaches when the ocean tide is low."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"MARSHTOMP is much faster at traveling through mud than it is at swimming. This POKéMON’s hindquarters exhibit obvious development, giving it the ability to walk on just its hind legs."},{"version":"emerald","text":"Its toughened hind legs enable it to stand upright. Because it weakens if its skin dries out, it replenishes fluids by playing in mud."},{"version":"firered","text":"It is at its best when on muddy ground with poor footing. It quickly overwhelms foes struggling in mud."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Its sturdy legs give it sure footing, even in mud. It burrows into dirt to sleep."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Living on muddy ground that provides poor footing has made its legs sturdy."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"The surface of Marshtomp’s body is enveloped by a thin, sticky film that enables it to live on land. This Pokémon plays in mud on beaches when the ocean tide is low."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Marshtomp is